SUMMARY:Rogê
LOCATION:Parlor Room\, 32 Masonic St\, Northampton\, MA 01060
DESCRIPTION:An homage to the golden era of samba Born Roger José Cury in R
 io de Janeiro\, Rogê (pronounced haw-zheh) spent more than a decade as a 
 fixture of Lapa\, Rio's bustling nightlife district\, where he held court 
 at the legendary samba club Carioca da Gema. He gained an avid following f
 or his swinging samba-funk tinged with Brazilian soul\, releasing seven so
 lo albums and earning a Latin Grammy nomination for Na Veia\, his collabor
 ation with samba legend Arlindo Cruz. He further raised his profile by co-
 writing the theme song for the 2016 Rio Olympic Games.\nhttps://theparlorr
 oom.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SV500000Bxr5BMAR\nFrom Pushp
 in Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://theparlorroom.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SV50000
 0Bxr5BMAR
