SUMMARY:Songwriter Series: Cricket Blue\, Ciarra Fragale\, Elijah Berlow
LOCATION:Parlor Room\, 32 Masonic St\, Northampton\, MA 01060
DESCRIPTION:Sweet Animal\, the sophomore album from acclaimed chamber folk 
 duo Cricket Blue (Laura Heaberlin and Taylor Smith)\, is a semi-continuous
 \, intricately arranged\, cyclical suite of songs that confront death\, lo
 ve\, grief\, and embodiment in the physical plane. “Sweet Animal is a re
 ference to your own body being a sweet animal\,” says Heaberlin. “Havi
 ng a tenderness toward your own physicality.” Featuring contributions fr
 om Goose drummer Cotter Ellis\, Clogs bassoonist Rachael Elliott\, members
  of the Vermont Symphony Orchestra\, and dozens of musicians from the regi
 on's classical\, folk\, and experimental scenes\, Cricket Blue balances ch
 amber-scale intricacy with communal warmth.\nhttps://theparlorroom.my.sale
 sforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SV500000CixtVMAR\nFrom Pushpin Western 
