SUMMARY:Jake Blount
LOCATION:Parlor Room\, 32 Masonic St\, Northampton\, MA 01060
DESCRIPTION:Jake Blount is a performer and scholar of Black folk music base
 d in Providence\, RI. Initially recognized for his skill as a string band 
 musician\, Blount has synthesized his scholarly and artistic pursuits into
  a diverse performance practice that has taken him to Carnegie Hall\, Newp
 ort Folk Festival\, NPR’s Tiny Desk\, and beyond. His albums\, released 
 on Free Dirt Records and Smithsonian Folkways Recordings\, have been featu
 red in best-of lists from NPR\, The New Yorker\, and Rolling Stone. His sc
 holarly publications include “Jail the Zombie: Black Banjoists\, Biopoli
 tics\, and Archives\,” published in Modern American History. He also ser
 ved as a music consultant for the movie Sinners\, and performed on the sou
 ndtrack of Ken Burns’s The American Revolution. Blount holds an A.M. in 
 Musicology and Ethnomusicology from Brown University\, where he is working
  toward a Ph.D. in the same and a second master’s degree in Anthropology
 . A new string band record is forthcoming in September 2026.\nhttps://thep
 arlorroom.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SV500000B7NnxMAF\nFrom
  Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://theparlorroom.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SV50000
 0B7NnxMAF
END:VEVENT
